Subject: vk: fall back to storage buffers when unsized UBO arrays are unsupported
Why: the shader backends emit uniform blocks whose last member is a runtime-sized
     array, which requires VK_EXT_shader_uniform_buffer_unsized_array. That
     extension was requested unconditionally (with a FIXME noting there was no
     fallback), so on drivers lacking it — every Qualcomm Adreno, i.e. every
     Snapdragon Android device — the feature struct is silently ignored and every
     graphics pipeline creation then fails with VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN, killing the RSX
     worker threads. Runtime-sized arrays are always legal in storage buffers, so
     emit the affected blocks as "readonly restrict buffer" and register them as
     storage descriptors when the extension is missing. The extension is now also
     actually requested (previously it was only chained as a feature struct) on
     drivers that expose it, so those keep the uniform-block path unchanged.
Upstream-status: candidate

